  "market_context": "During a downtrend on GBPUSD 15-minute chart, price momentum slowed (angle flattened), leading to a pullback. The analyst identified a pivot point where price retraced to the 0.50 Fibonacci level and formed a reversal candlestick pattern near the 21-period moving average.",
  "key_observation": "Price slowed its downward cascade, retraced precisely to the 0.50 Fibonacci level (1.34974), and formed a three line strike pattern rejecting off the 21 MA, signaling trend continuation short entry.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Noted that price momentum was slowing — the downtrend angle flattened and price stopped cascading down.",
    "Step 2: Drew Fibonacci retracement from swing high ~1.36583 to swing low ~1.35482, identifying the 0.50 level at 1.34974 as the retracement zone.",
    "Step 3: Observed a three line strike pattern (three consecutive candles up, followed by one engulfing bearish candle) forming at the pivot near the 21 MA.",
    "Step 4: Confirmed rejection off the 21-period moving average, using it as confluence for a trend continuation short entry targeting TP1."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "When downtrend momentum slows, a retracement to the 0.50 Fib level combined with a three line strike rejection at a dynamic support like the 21 MA offers high-probability trend continuation entries.",
